  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Complete small timber tower gazebo: four tall exposed posts, open raised square platform, steep stair with separate treads/stringers/handrails, vertical platform balusters with a real stair entry, bracing and green pyramidal sheet-metal roof with underside rafters. Shared wood_plain and metal_standing_seam graphs, four authored LODs and no private texture atlas, copied photograph pixels or attached tree geometry. Hidden joinery and exact scale remain original photo-led approximations. Photo-led platform2.15m square, upper floor modelY2.45m, eave4.65m and roof peak5.4m. Four main posts follow individually sampled ground and extend.18m into it. Stair run2.6m, width.95m, 9open treads from original soil modelY0.25112494991566336m to platform. Handrails/platform rail1.0m above walking surfaces. Exact post diameters, tread/log/baluster census, roof pitch and historical levels/accessibility are approximate. The inner roof-bearing ring is seated on post tops at modelY4.773076923076924m, above the lower overhanging eave, and hip rafters follow the actual roof pitch. Retained Protomaps20261020/Mapzen201x201/6m standard extract. Outside control[-2.5,0] sets datum198.23757107381198m. Four post ground offsets[-0.07934965518876425,-0.106392250622946,0.018416897355848505,0.04679499927158304]m; whole platform sits about2.4m above the highest sampled post foot. Original ground remains beneath platform, stair, supports and approaches; solid posts/stringer ends seat into soil without cutouts. No flattening, new water or bespoke terrain. The map lacks this small footprint and final trail connection; exact orientation, scale and soil/footing details remain approximate. Museum and Commons photos establish the exterior silhouette. The map provides only a named point and a path about6.9m away; it does not establish footprint, dimensions or compass facing. Front assignment and scale are deliberately approximate;30degrees is an authoring uncertainty estimate, not a measured angular bound. The small final foot trail is not represented in retained data and is not fabricated. Tree-obscured rear details, exact baluster/tread census, joinery, roof section and historical levels/accessibility remain reconstructed. Other estate buildings/trees remain independent context."
  },
